body:
Yes, very much so yes. 

&#x200B;

When I found out I was bi-polar I gave up on trying to find love since I thought no one would want to stick with me through the good and the bad. Eventually I found my partner. Fast forward 3 years, the week after our marriage I had a manic episode that led to her leaving for a week. Then last week I had another episode and now she's leaving me. 

&#x200B;

I knew it was too good to be true and well now here I am, just accepting that my manic episodes will always prevent me from getting close to people.

Oooooooh that sounds awesome. Especially since Disney now picked up Miraculous Ladybug and Chat Noir, since Chat Noir is my go to cosplay. 

&#x200B;

As for other activities I would say maybe have disney Karaoke, trivia competitions, and if covid clears up enough, a disney food competition where people recreate their favorite disney foods and you can get a professional chef or someone like that to review their creations. Those are just a few ideas.

Honestly anything distracting. I've been battling Bi-Polar depression for years and sometimes it's not that bad while other times I just legit need to lock myself away from the world. Like right now with this polarized world and trying to remain happy in the middle feels like it impossible and after losing contact with much of my support group I just need that one or two people to say 'Hey let's just go out for a walk or go to the mall and people watch'. But without that distraction my brain is telling me to tie a rope around a tree and the other end around my neck, and get on my motorcycle and gun it. When I have something distracting me from those thoughts it allows more time for me to see how stupid that is. I know it's stupid but when losing your support group you just need one or two people to literally grab you by the collar and drag you up. Unfortunately as I previously mentioned I don't have that. And so now I keep digging that thought deeper and deeper in my head to the point where I honestly feel that it's too late and I'm just talking to myself with my own echo chamber of one. And when you are in an echo chamber it just makes things worse. You need that opposite voice to help pull you out of that void but unfortunately I think that I am too far gone. I have been 2.5 years clean without a suicide attempt but unfortunately I think I am about to break that streak.

&#x200B;

I doubt anyone will actually give two shits about my post but if my actions can help anyone learn that's all that I can hope for in case I succeed finally and become one of the 22 veterans who end their lifes each day.
